# openOODA — agent token discipline (product CLI)

Token minimization is a **product capability** of openOODA (`ooda` / `oodac`),
not an external skill. Use the CLI; do not invent parallel agent workflows.

## Product commands (built-in)

```bash
# from ooda/
./bin/ooda help
./bin/ooda check <file.oo>
./bin/ooda build <file.oo> [-o out]
./bin/ooda run <file.oo>
./bin/ooda test <file.oo>                 # same as run
./bin/ooda dump tokens|ast|check <file.oo>
./bin/ooda outline <file.oo>
./bin/ooda reflect <file.oo> [sym]
./bin/ooda patch <file.oo> --replace-fn <n> --with <body>
./bin/ooda fix <file.oo> [--yes]          # asks unless --yes

# residual (fail closed): context digest health err-digest pack pkg add
# compiler
./oodac/oodac check|outline|reflect <file.oo>
```

## Hard rules (token traps)

| Never auto-read | Why |
|-----------------|-----|
| `~/.cache/ooda-tmp/**/all*.c` | ~700KB pure emit |
| Full `openOODA/ROADMAP.oot` | use `ooda digest` residual slice |
| Full `emit-c` stdout | use `ooda health` / outline |
| 500+ line gcc logs | use `ooda err-digest` |

## Never copy CLI onto compiler

`./bin/ooda` is the product CLI. `./oodac/oodac` is the compiler.
Never copy, install, or overwrite `bin/ooda` onto `oodac/oodac`.

Tell them apart with `strings`:
- compiler: `oodac: usage: [--backend c|wasm|llvm|x86] tokens|ast|check|...`
- CLI: `pure .oo product CLI` / `ooda 0.199.0-alpha`

Running the CLI as `oodac check` is a fork bomb (each check execs itself).

## Work loop

1. `ooda outline` on 1–3 files (digest/context are residual)
2. `ooda check` the file you edit
3. Minimal repro; edit; smoke with **exit code + last line only**
4. Leave-off ≤15 lines

## Measured

`c_emit_ty.oo` outline ≈ **1.3%** of full source bytes.
`context` reports `est_tokens_full` vs `est_tokens_slice`.
